```deck:slide
title: Overrides
```

## Per-slide titles

This slide overrides the footer title via its own `deck:slide` block.

Everything else falls back to the deck title.

---

```deck:slide
title: Live shell
```

## Real processes, live

<tty id="counter" persist title="Live counter" rows="8" cols="44">
i=0; while :; do echo "tick $i"; i=$((i + 1)); sleep 1; done
</tty>

This box runs a real shell command, streaming its output.

---

```deck:slide
title: It keeps running
```

## The same process, one slide later

The counter is `persist` with `id=counter`, so it was **not** restarted —
it kept counting across the slide change.

<tty id="counter" persist title="Live counter" rows="8" cols="44">
i=0; while :; do echo "tick $i"; i=$((i + 1)); sleep 1; done
</tty>

---

```deck:slide
title: Colors
```

## Colors, like a native terminal

<tty title="Ephemeral (no id)" rows="8" cols="44">
printf '\033[31mred\033[0m \033[32mgreen\033[0m \033[33myellow\033[0m \033[34mblue\033[0m\n'
for n in 1 2 3 4 5; do echo "line $n"; sleep 0.4; done
echo done
</tty>

No `id`, so this one is killed when you leave — and restarts if you return.

